{"title":"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the set of all fractions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e32f96b310bbe6cd6981b6c1da83fe7905ea3116.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"12\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. How many of these fractions have the property that if both numerator and denominator are increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the value of the fraction is increased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/5/2b56bd637cb2c936d539be1b5000a64a898af389.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c254268ca4a5d58cb8278dfd22ef798652bd1fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }0\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }1\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }2\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }\\text{infinitely many}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"453\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You can create the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c86d9ee95fe68aaf28d6d87461954fbc8e772e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+1}{y+1}=\\frac{11x}{10y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"101\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Cross multiplying and combining like terms gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/9/b69bfd92e44a61b3eee27de867dcdeb4f93298da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy + 11x - 10y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>This can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/c/d8c748649b701f01be2f705490d6c7efd23e1eab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x - 10)(y + 11) = -110$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae4fd68f44ac9b909f8d91f9d498de5759bb45b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6267cf18ccdbddb223019a94263e5b80bafe617.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/d/e7d330b5007085f3ddea5c7b982fc8d6d03b3558.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 10&gt; -10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"106\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/2426c21e40a76a08fcf00a98c2c6e93c3624765d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + 11 &gt; 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Using the factors of 110, we can get the factor pairs: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8fb62c4db1a1fa0b0389195ecd0c7d03369e2e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 110),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/0/ff0532723e0773116898dab99414447688f25a63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2, 55),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/c/d1cd2b290bdab78481f9a06ff024626f4c4cd20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5, 22).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>But we can't stop here because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be relatively prime.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/7/5f788b31517ad7fd558eb149fd621353e5fd14fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1, 110)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a7a2005b67ab81ee5ff231b2f370f1d71ebe1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/c/58c021c64fecaaf4d6a642c4ab3fb106f1598398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are not relatively prime, so this doesn't work.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/3/6d3cd12d31677995bcb39e0282b4abffdd212e99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2, 55)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/4/62434ae80ca145c20f0fbc7563f5151371ed163c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6ba585c0c81fc1f3f70c362d5806356278f287a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. This doesn't work.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/d/68d28bf0f875ca05d4d0ed7dcd35c78637e16013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-5, 22)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/3/c832e4ebb5fc13830ee1f7897c5ac56e83f94e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. This does work.\n</p><p>We found one valid solution so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e101201addd96f637069ef5899fa2b44223efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The condition required is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0fd410f63e9ddc3d86483822a62651f2a5cb65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+1}{y+1}=\\frac{11}{10}\\cdot\\frac{x}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"121\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Observe that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12ecf0abf79cc52efa674d7e5b935e49cd90f413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+1 &gt; \\frac{11}{10}\\cdot x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a1b9d5cec741422bfb37f91db47fd7514f5377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>By multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/0/e00997435b70ac3c4293ac773a5e6e2e5f691d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y+1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"43\" height=\"37\" /> and simplifying we can rewrite the condition as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8427d6f143a4af41120b0f340ebfbe0f4ff99cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{11x}{10-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are integer, this only has solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee7ab6aba0d6734ced8bb7bf5bfad36edd3dde0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\{5,8,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />.  However, only the first yields a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that is relative prime to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>There is only one valid solution so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e101201addd96f637069ef5899fa2b44223efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>So from this question, we can get \\(\\frac{x+1}{y+1} = \\frac{11x}{10y}\\). We can transform this equation into \\(x + 11 \\cdot \\left( \\frac{x}{y} \\right) = 10\\). Two numbers are added to get 10, and one of them, \\(x\\), is a positive and prime integer. So the other number also has to be a positive integer. Therefore, \\(11 \\cdot \\left( \\frac{x}{y} \\right)\\) is a positive integer. The only possibility of this being true is when \\(y\\) and 11 cancel out, leaving a singular \\(x\\). So \\(y = 11\\) and \\(x + x = 10\\). Therefore, \\(y = 11\\) and \\(x = 5\\).\n</p><p>~POISONPOISSON\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p7g0hTxE9I8\">https://youtu.be/p7g0hTxE9I8</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A\">2015 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017055721\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.091 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 324/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7976/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.528      1 -total\n 59.82%    7.494      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 39.18%    4.909      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13943:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017055721 and revision id 237205. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}